Proposed changes in the [SOP|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/2407825593/BOLT-IMS-006-SOP-002.007+Driver+Acts+of+Discrimination]:

h3. Driver Refuses Assistance Animal

An event in which the driver refused to pick up a rider with a service animal {color:#ff5630}-(granted that the rider had the proper documentation).-{color}

*Queries for the reporting user/passenger:*

* Ask the reporting user to describe the issue;
* {color:#ff5630}-Ask the reporting to send us the documentation of having an assistance animal;-{color}
* If the reporting user mentions they have video or photo proof, ask them to provide it.
* In addition, ask for the following information to identify the order if not already provided:
** Screenshot of the trip in their Bolt app;
** The date and time of the trip;
** The phone number of the reporting user.

*Queries for the reported user/driver:*

* Inform the reported user about the suspension on their account; and that you are contacting them regarding a trip (provide them with the date);
* Ask the reported user why the reporting user might’ve made a report like that;
* Ask the reported user if they are exempt from carrying assistance animals:
** If they are exempt, ask them to provide documentation.

