Hi [~accountid:608a8089248ef60073a1fb22] ,

can you please clarify what do you mean by “active“ and “passive“ data in this specific scenario? Based on what datapoints related to user’s localisation exactly would you plan to send out this communication? 

This is quite complex project privacy-wise, and I’d appreciate if you could please provide additional context here, but general legal requirements for localisation-based marketing are as follows:

* collecting any information about user’s location when the app is closed would constitute very high privacy risk;
* under GDPR using localisation for marketing purposes would require consent. You can utilise existing consent modules in Bolt App for this purposes;
* in Bolt privacy policy we state that Bolt only uses user’s localisation for service-related purposes, so if you’d like to proceed with this project both SE and DK privacy policies would need to be updated;
* under article 35 of GDPR, processing activities that involve processing data at large scale should be subject to documented data protection impact assessment which is a type of formal and documented privacy analysis. While this requirement won’t materialise for the proof-of-concept stage, if this project will be considered to be rolled out on broader scale, then appropriate assessment would be mandatory ([this|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/3848767649/Procedures+for+the+Data+Protection+Impact+Assessment] page is still in work-in-progress but provides some overview on the process);
* and finally, as with all push notifications, those would also require end user granting appropriate permissions on their device to receive such communication.



Kind regards,

Adriana

