* Will the first test require any development? Or will this be a 1-click test?  --- Yes, we want to do 2 tests:
** The idea is to remove the “i” indicator, so the 1st test is to verify that it does not change anything significantly - users still opening the category details screen at similar rate and no changes to main metrics; We have a hypothesis that the “i” is not necessary, so we want to do a short , max 1 week test to verify; 
** After verifying the removal of “i”, we then test, the best way to show the combination of surge and recommended labels; - 3 paths - control, treatment 1, treatment 2, treatment 3; To see, if there are any differences in main KPI’s and taps to open category details; 
* Will there be any additional analytics events required for the 2nd experiment? - we don’t need any additional events, we already have the select category tap and category details expanded; 

This means that there are 2 separate targeting parameters - one removes the “i”, another provides the surge and recommended label visuals;

