So the investigation is finished. Right now is not possible for us to get metrics for prometheus. 

# the First issue was that Spectrum metrics via GraphQL for us are disabled. Enabled by CF Support via request. 
# After getting access to graphql API, found a lot of useful metrics. But getting graphql schema was work for me only via this: [https://github.com/graphql/graphiql|https://github.com/graphql/graphiql|smart-link]  
# Query example

{noformat}query SpectrumBitsPerPorts
{
  viewer
  {
    accounts(filter: {accountTag: "6dfc700f0a2a90d894aab0e8a81c7719"}) {
      spectrumNetworkAnalyticsAdaptiveGroups
      (filter: 
        {
          datetime_gt: "2022-07-03T16:07:05Z", 
          datetime_lt: "2022-07-03T17:07:05Z",
          direction: "ingress"

        }, 
        limit:10000

        ) 
      {
        dimensions{destinationPort, outcome, direction,mitigationSystem

        }
        sum{bits}
      }
    }
  }
}{noformat}

Query answer: 

{noformat}            {
              "dimensions": {
                "destinationPort": 1883,
                "direction": "ingress",
                "mitigationSystem": "",
                "outcome": "pass"
              },
              "sum": {
                "bits": 58476480000
              }
            },
            {
              "dimensions": {
                "destinationPort": 5608,
                "direction": "ingress",
                "mitigationSystem": "",
                "outcome": "pass"
              },
              "sum": {
                "bits": 150640000
              }
            },
            {
              "dimensions": {
                "destinationPort": 80,
                "direction": "ingress",
                "mitigationSystem": "",
                "outcome": "pass"
              },
              "sum": {
                "bits": 5120000
              }
            },{noformat}

So in theory we could get statistics per port and passed traffic with information about blocking + it’s also possible to get geo and other networking information regarding this. Buuut, no chance to put this information to the prometheus. 

What options we had: 

# Use one of opensource cloudflare exporter like this: [https://github.com/lablabs/cloudflare-exporter|https://github.com/lablabs/cloudflare-exporter|smart-link]  . But checked all available exporter on github no one of them support spectrum dataset..
# Another option was to use clean graphql exporter with support of any graphql request like this: [https://github.com/ricardbejarano/graphql_exporter|https://github.com/ricardbejarano/graphql_exporter|smart-link] .
But it doesn’t work properly in the case of CF. Run locally prom stack, it parses every JSON object to different data. It’s how query what describe before looks like: 

!image-20220728-121246.png|width=1779,height=192!

And with graph it looks like this: 

!image-20220728-121354.png|width=1777,height=339!

So it’s not possible with such data to build any information dashboard. 
3. Another option as last resort was graphql data source for grafana: [https://grafana.com/grafana/plugins/fifemon-graphql-datasource/|https://grafana.com/grafana/plugins/fifemon-graphql-datasource/|smart-link] But it with this plugin wasn’t able to parse response from CF, don’t have an idea why it does not work, but doesn’t spend time on it, due to use such datasource quite unflexible for us. 


So what we may do with this… Write own exporter, but it’s a quite big scope for our team, not sure that with our capacity we may afford it to ourself. Another option is to ask BEPL to prepare such a thing for us. But it should be discussed first with our EM. 

So close task for now, maybe we will back to it when it will be really critical for us.

